                <pb facs="0945" n="849" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg849"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.51/92: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schuyler</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-09-07T20:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 7,
                                1921—8 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 8—10:10
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>44. Representative of Mr. Keith signed today with the Salvadorean Government
                    contract for temporary loan $250,000 secured by 41 percent import duties. The
                    Government grants extension of loan and bank options 5 months from their
                    expiration dates.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schuyler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
